s model was conducted by MODELLER program. (a) Overall structure of <italic>M. pneumoniae</italic> enolase with containing Mg<sup>2+</sup> cofactor. (b) Comparison of enolase structure among three diferrent organisms.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="97320630003018F3"/></fig><fig id="F4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Model of <italic>M. pneumoniae</italic> enolase-human plasminogen complex interaction. (a) H-bond represent in red line. (b) Electrostatic surfaces, a color ramp was calculated, which positive potential charges in blue, negative values in red, and intermediate values in white by using PyMol (<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://pymol.sourceforge.net/">http://pymol.sourceforge.net/</ext-link>).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="97320630003018F4"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>